  "task_version": 2,
  "query": "I fly long-haul for work every month, pack a single small backpack, and wear glasses I can't take off mid-flight. Big over-ears feel like the obvious answer for engine noise, but they eat half my bag and I've read glasses arms break the seal so the noise cancelling stops working properly. Is that a real physical problem or overblown? Would compact on-ears or good earbuds actually serve a glasses wearer better for ten hours in the air? I'd love to hear from frequent flyers who wear glasses too, and then a pick that fits my bag and my face.",
